of activity and dysfunction-related genes in responding patients, while in clinically non-responding patients, NK cells showed an increased cytotoxic transcriptional profile early upon treatment. These data reveal the immunological changes in response to dual PD-1 and CTLA4 blockade, including a parallel remodeling of presumed tumor-reactive T cell compartments in responding patients, and indicate that the presence of an activated Treg compartment at baseline may be associated with response.","gpl":"18573;21697","gse":"232240","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing; Other","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2023/08/07","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM7324304","title":"CF39579_pre_27, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324307","title":"CF39581_pre_31, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324313","title":"CF71333_post_39, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324296","title":"CF30578_pre_15, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324310","title":"CF39616_pre_36, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324302","title":"CF71328_post_21, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324311","title":"CF71327_post_36, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324299","title":"CF71325_post_17, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324294","title":"IMCISION, scRNAseq"},{"accession":"GSM7324305","title":"CF71330_post_27, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324297","title":"CF71326_post_15, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324308","title":"CF71331_post_29, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324303","title":"CF71329_post_22, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324306","title":"CF39580_pre_29, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324300","title":"CF39574_pre_21, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324312","title":"CF39622_pre_39, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324309","title":"CF71332_post_31, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324301","title":"CF39575_pre_22, bulk TCR-seq"},{"accession":"GSM7324295","title":"IMCISION, meta data (scTCRseq and scRNAseq)"},{"accession":"GSM7324298","title":"CF39571_pre_17, bulk TCR-seq"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":20,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["37548431"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE232nnn/GSE232240/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA971417"},"200227919":{"uid":"200227919","accession":"GSE227919","gds":"","title":"Total RNA sequencing reveals gene expression and microbial alterations shared by oral pre-malignant lesions and cancer.","summary":"Head and neck cancers are a complex malignancy comprising multiple anatomical sites, with cancer of the oral cavity ranking among the deadliest and most disfiguring cancers globally. Oral cancer (OC) constitutes a subset of head and neck cancer cases, presenting primarily as tobacco- and alcohol-associated oral squamous cell carcinoma (OSCC), with a 5-year survival rate of ~65%, partly due to the lack of early detection and effective treatments. OSCC arises from premalignant lesions (PMLs) in the oral cavity through a multi-step series of clinical and histopathological stages, including varying degrees of epithelial dysplasia. To gain insights into the molecular mechanisms associated with the progression of PMLs to OSCC, we profiled the whole transcriptome of 66 human PMLs comprising leukoplakia with dysplasia and hyper­keratosis non-reactive (HkNR) pathologies, alongside healthy controls and OSCC. Our data revealed that PMLs were enriched in gene signatures associated with cellular plasticity, such as partial EMT (p-EMT) phenotypes, and with immune response. Integrated analyses of the host transcriptome and microbiome further highlighted a significant association between differential microbial abundance and PML pathway activity, suggesting a contribution of the oral microbiome towards PML evolution to OSCC. Collectively, this study reveals molecular processes associated with PML progression that may help early diagnosis and disease interception at an early stage.","gpl":"18573","gse":"227919","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2023/08/07","suppfile":"CSV, TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM7110938","title":"HkNR [MK_20]"},{"accession":"GSM7110921","title":"Control [MK_50]"},{"accession":"GSM7110958","title":"Dysplasia [MK_13]"},{"accession":"GSM7110918","title":"Dysplasia [MK_35]"},{"accession":"GSM7110961","title":"Dysplasia [MK_B6A]"},{"accession":"GSM7110981","title":"HkNR [MK_EOG_009]"},{"accession":"GSM7110935","title":"Dysplasia [MK_12]"},{"accession":"GSM7110941","title":"HkNR [MK_33]"},{"accession":"GSM7110978","title":"Control [MK_EOG_001]"},{"accession":"GSM7110967","title":"Control [MK_B-0005]"},{"accession":"GSM7110964","title":"Control [MK_B-0002]"},{"accession":"GSM7110947","title":"Cancer [MK_40]"},{"accession":"GSM7110927","title":"HkNR [MK_43]"},{"accession":"GSM7110944","title":"HkNR [MK_23]"},{"accession":"GSM7110924","title":"HkNR [MK_31]"},{"accession":"GSM7110950","title":"Control [MK_24]"},{"accession":"GSM7110970","title":"Dysplasia [MK_B-013]"},{"accession":"GSM7110976","title":"Cancer [MK_B-0022]"},{"accession":"GSM7110936","title":"Dysplasia [MK_17]"},{"accession":"GSM7110973","title":"Cancer [MK_B-018]"},{"accession":"GSM7110930","title":"Cancer [MK_5]"},{"accession":"GSM7110956","title":"Control [MK_3]"},{"accession":"GSM7110939","title":"Control [MK_26]"},{"accession":"GSM7110953","title":"HkNR [MK_36]"},{"accession":"GSM7110982","title":"Control [MK_EOG_012]"},{"accession":"GSM7110965","title":"Dysplasia [MK_B-0003]"},{"accession":"GSM7110919","title":"HkNR [MK_39]"},{"accession":"GSM7110933","title":"Dysplasia [MK_9]"},{"accession":"GSM7110922","title":"Dysplasia [MK_52]"},{"accession":"GSM7110942","title":"Cancer [MK_16]"},{"accession":"GSM7110979","title":"Control [MK_EOG_004]"},{"accession":"GSM7110948","title":"Dys