l line. T-HEp3 is a human epidermoid carcinoma, which grows on chorioallantoic membrane and metastasizes with high efficiency into the organs of chick embryo. Upon serial passage for more than 40 times in vitro, T-HEp3 loses tumorigenic and metastatic potential and termed as dormant D-HEp3. This is an ideal cell line model system to study cancer dormancy.","gpl":"16791","gse":"181837","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2023/04/27","suppfile":"CSV, XLSX","samples":[{"accession":"GSM5512737","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si1-AZA+atRA rep2"},{"accession":"GSM5512740","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si2-AZA+atRA rep1"},{"accession":"GSM5512734","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si1-DMSO rep1"},{"accession":"GSM5512731","title":"T-HEp3-scr-DMSO control rep2"},{"accession":"GSM5512732","title":"T-HEp3-scr-AZA+atRA rep1"},{"accession":"GSM5512735","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si1-DMSO rep2"},{"accession":"GSM5512738","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si2-DMSO rep1"},{"accession":"GSM5512733","title":"T-HEp3-scr AZA+atRA rep2"},{"accession":"GSM5512730","title":"T-HEp3-scr--DMSO control rep1"},{"accession":"GSM5512741","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si2-AZA+atRA rep2"},{"accession":"GSM5512736","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si1-AZA+atRA rep1"},{"accession":"GSM5512739","title":"T-HEp3-NR2F1si2-DMSO rep2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[{"relationtype":"SRA","targetobject":"SRP331964","targetftplink":"ftp://ftp-trace.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra/sra-instant/reads/ByStudy/sra/SRP/SRP331/SRP331964/"}],"n_samples":12,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["37267946"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE181nnn/GSE181837/","geo2r":"yes","bioproject":"PRJNA753542"},"200205308":{"uid":"200205308","accession":"GSE205308","gds":"","title":"Deep learning for explainable prediction of HPV-status in head and neck cancer using transcriptome data organized as pathway treemaps","summary":"We propose a convolutional neural network (CNN) model predicting HPV-status in head and neck cancer from transcriptome data allowing identification of molecular pathways driving individual classifier decisions.  The CNN was trained on transcriptome data from 264 (13% HPV-positive) and tested on 85 (25% HPV-positive) patients after transformation into 2D-treemaps representing molecular pathways. Model stability was assessed by shuffling pathways within 2D-images. Grad-CAM saliency was used to quantify pathways contribution to CNN decisions. For comparison, a logistic regression model was generated.  The CNN achieved ROC-AUC/PR-AUC of 0.96/0.90 for all treemap variants. Saliency heatmaps consistently found KRAS-, spermatogenesis-, bile acid metabolism- and inflammatory-signaling as most informative for classification of HPV-positive-, and MYC-targets-, epithelial-mesenchymal transition and protein-secretion pathways for HPV-negative patients. The regression-based 18-gene model achieved a ROC-AUC/PR-AUC of 0.97/0.97.  We present a high-performance explainable CNN-model from transcriptome data of a typically sized oncological cohort providing molecular pathway information at the individual level.","gpl":"20301","gse":"205308","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2023/04/24","suppfile":"TXT","samples":[{"accession":"GSM6210043","title":"LMU_Pat_19"},{"accession":"GSM6210089","title":"LMU_Pat_65"},{"accession":"GSM6210069","title":"LMU_Pat_45"},{"accession":"GSM6210086","title":"LMU_Pat_62"},{"accession":"GSM6210066","title":"LMU_Pat_42"},{"accession":"GSM6210083","title":"LMU_Pat_59"},{"accession":"GSM6210063","title":"LMU_Pat_39"},{"accession":"GSM6210046","title":"LMU_Pat_22"},{"accession":"GSM6210026","title":"LMU_Pat_02"},{"accession":"GSM6210034","title":"LMU_Pat_10"},{"accession":"GSM6210080","title":"LMU_Pat_5